# VS Code REST Client (humao.rest-client): click "Send Request" above a request.
# Send requests individually, in order within each section. Named responses capture IDs.
# Workers must use DEMO_FAILURES_ENABLED=true for the three fixed failure tasks.
# AI requests may take up to 130 seconds on a cold local Ollama model.
# Quick-demo IDs reference this machine's existing database; use fresh flows after a reset.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@aiUrl = http://localhost:8085
@verifiedFailedRun = 3aa118dc-d9ea-48ce-b9ba-1b24e22882d4
@verifiedAnalysis = b746b2a4-7346-4ade-b667-fff197a28f38

### API health
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### AI health
GET {{aiUrl}}/actuator/health

### Quick demo: read the persisted failure from the verified local demo
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/runs/{{verifiedFailedRun}}/failure-analysis

### Quick demo: historical timeout matches, excluding the current run
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/runs/{{verifiedFailedRun}}/similar-incidents?topK=3

### Quick demo: evidence-backed synthesis (cached when evidence is unchanged)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/runs/{{verifiedFailedRun}}/similar-incidents/synthesize?topK=3
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Quick demo: exact factual snapshot referenced by its analysis ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/failure-analyses/{{verifiedAnalysis}}

### Manual workflow: persist a normal DAG; no execution yet
# @name createWorkflow
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workflows
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "VS Code parallel invoice demo",
  "description": "Simulated tasks with parallel branches and a join",
  "defaultFailurePolicy": "FAIL_FAST",
  "tasks": [
    {"taskId": "download", "name": "downloadOrders", "maxRetries": 2, "dependsOn": []},
    {"taskId": "validate", "name": "validateOrders", "maxRetries": 2, "dependsOn": ["download"]},
    {"taskId": "invoiceA", "name": "invoiceBatch1", "maxRetries": 2, "dependsOn": ["validate"]},
    {"taskId": "invoiceB", "name": "invoiceBatch2", "maxRetries": 2, "dependsOn": ["validate"]},
    {"taskId": "upload", "name": "uploadInvoices", "maxRetries": 2, "dependsOn": ["invoiceA", "invoiceB"]},
    {"taskId": "notify", "name": "sendNotification", "maxRetries": 2, "dependsOn": ["upload"]}
  ]
}

### Retrieve the persisted manual workflow
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workflows/{{createWorkflow.response.body.$.id}}

### Explicitly execute the manual workflow through the existing engine
# @name executeWorkflow
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workflows/{{createWorkflow.response.body.$.id}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "VS Code manual execution"}

### Check execution; repeat until status is COMPLETE
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/jobs/{{executeWorkflow.response.body.$.id}}

### AI generation: preview only; inspect validation.valid and the DAG
# @name generateWorkflow
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/workflows/generate
Content-Type: application/json

{"prompt": "Create a simulated NOOP workflow that downloads customer orders, validates them, generates two invoice batches in parallel, uploads them after both batches finish, and sends a notification. Use only supported NOOP tasks."}

### Retrieve the preview; no workflow is persisted yet
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/workflows/proposals/{{generateWorkflow.response.body.$.proposalId}}

### Explicit approval: send only after reviewing a valid proposal
# @name approveWorkflow
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/workflows/proposals/{{generateWorkflow.response.body.$.proposalId}}/approve

### Retrieve the approved normal workflow
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workflows/{{approveWorkflow.response.body.$.id}}

### Explicitly execute the approved workflow; approval itself does not execute it
# @name executeApprovedWorkflow
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workflows/{{approveWorkflow.response.body.$.id}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "VS Code approved AI workflow execution"}

### Inspect execution
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/jobs/{{executeApprovedWorkflow.response.body.$.id}}

### Incident A: create a controlled connection timeout
# @name createTimeoutA
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "VS Code timeout A", "failurePolicy": "FAIL_FAST", "tasks": [{"taskId": "timeout", "name": "demoConnectionTimeout", "maxRetries": 2, "dependsOn": []}]}

### Repeat until FAILED; task should be DEAD_LETTERED with retryCount 2
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/jobs/{{createTimeoutA.response.body.$.id}}

### Analyze A only after its failed execution has settled
# @name analyzeTimeoutA
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/runs/{{createTimeoutA.response.body.$.id}}/analyze-failure
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Explicitly index A; safe to repeat (insertedCount becomes 0)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/failure-analyses/{{analyzeTimeoutA.response.body.$.analysisId}}/index
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Incident B: similar downstream timeout
# @name createTimeoutB
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "VS Code timeout B", "failurePolicy": "FAIL_FAST", "tasks": [{"taskId": "timeout", "name": "demoDownstreamTimeout", "maxRetries": 2, "dependsOn": []}]}

### Repeat until FAILED before analyzing
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/jobs/{{createTimeoutB.response.body.$.id}}

### Analyze B; repeating reuses the stored analysis ID and facts
# @name analyzeTimeoutB
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/runs/{{createTimeoutB.response.body.$.id}}/analyze-failure
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Explicitly index B before searching
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/failure-analyses/{{analyzeTimeoutB.response.body.$.analysisId}}/index
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Search B: inspect scores and real run/task/analysis references
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/runs/{{createTimeoutB.response.body.$.id}}/similar-incidents?topK=3

### Ask whether this happened before; citations must come from retrieved matches
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/runs/{{createTimeoutB.response.body.$.id}}/similar-incidents/synthesize?topK=3
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Read B's persisted facts and interpretation, without a model call
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/runs/{{createTimeoutB.response.body.$.id}}/failure-analysis

### Inspect current DLQ evidence; replay is deliberately omitted from this collection
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dlq?page=0&size=20

### Optional unrelated incident: JSON failure
# @name createJsonFailure
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "VS Code JSON failure", "failurePolicy": "FAIL_FAST", "tasks": [{"taskId": "json", "name": "demoInvalidJson", "maxRetries": 2, "dependsOn": []}]}

### Repeat until FAILED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/jobs/{{createJsonFailure.response.body.$.id}}

### Analyze JSON failure
# @name analyzeJsonFailure
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/runs/{{createJsonFailure.response.body.$.id}}/analyze-failure
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Index JSON failure
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/failure-analyses/{{analyzeJsonFailure.response.body.$.analysisId}}/index
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### JSON failures should not retrieve the timeout incidents at threshold 0.93
# Other JSON failures may match if you have run this section before.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/runs/{{createJsonFailure.response.body.$.id}}/similar-incidents?topK=3

### Invalid top-K should return 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/runs/{{verifiedFailedRun}}/similar-incidents?topK=6

### Successful execution cannot be analyzed as a failure (409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/runs/{{executeWorkflow.response.body.$.id}}/analyze-failure
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Missing run should return 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/jobs/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### API request/search metrics; Grafana: http://localhost:3000/d/conductor-requests
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/prometheus

### Copilot: read existing failure analysis (does not generate another analysis)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/copilot/query
Content-Type: application/json

{"question":"Why did this run fail?","jobId":"{{verifiedFailedRun}}"}

### Copilot: real historical incident evidence
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/copilot/query
Content-Type: application/json

{"question":"Have we seen this before?","jobId":"{{verifiedFailedRun}}"}

### Copilot: deterministic recorded retry counts
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/copilot/query
Content-Type: application/json

{"question":"How many retries happened?","jobId":"{{verifiedFailedRun}}"}

### Copilot: mutation refusal, no execution changes
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/copilot/query
Content-Type: application/json

{"question":"Retry this task.","jobId":"{{verifiedFailedRun}}"}

### Local model operation metrics
GET {{aiUrl}}/actuator/prometheus
